solutions.explanation:
Start with the innermost square root, since its value determines what is inside the next root. The symbol \(\sqrt{a}\) means the nonnegative square root of \(a\). Because \(2^2=4\), we have \(\sqrt{4}=2\). Therefore
\[
\sqrt{16\sqrt{8\sqrt{4}}}
=\sqrt{16\sqrt{8\cdot2}}
=\sqrt{16\cdot4}
=\sqrt{64}
=8.
\]
The value is \(\boxed{8}\), choice \(\boxed{\text{C}}\).
